  arms        : strict only, meaning torch's DEFAULT for this backend.
                On ROCm that default is off, but CDNA3 does have an XF32
                matrix mode that the same allow_tf32 switch reaches, so
                this is strict FP32 by default rather than by assertion.
                An XF32 arm is OWED here the way tf32 is measured on CUDA.
  bf16 arm    : both operands torch.bfloat16, product in bf16 (allow_tf32 off).

